# Eutopia -- pilot of the post-run10 policy fixes (input scaling, pre-activation
# clamp, head weight decay, clipped lambda), RL (pg) vs PERL (pepg), social + eo.
#
# 36 jobs = 2 agents x 3 seeds x 6 combos
#   (rawlsian_maximin / fairness_lagrangian / social_welfare) x (social, eo)
#
# This pilot TRAINS from scratch: WEIGHTS_CAMPAIGN is deliberately NOT set, so
# each job runs Phase 1 with the fixed loan_simulator/ code and then deploys.
# Short episode budget (200 train / 500 deploy) -- the point is to confirm the
# degenerate basins are gone before spending a full-scale campaign.
#
# Submit:
#   export N_SEEDS=3 CAMPAIGN=fixpilot TRAIN_EPISODES=200 DEPLOY_EPISODES=500
#   condor_submit_bid 25 cluster/pilot_fix.sub
#
# Verify when condor_q is empty (expect 18 checkpoints per agent):
#   ~/eutopia-venv/bin/python3 cluster/verify_run.py --root ~/eutopia_runs/fixpilot --seeds 3 --diagnose
#   ~/eutopia-venv/bin/python3 cluster/probe_policies.py --root ~/eutopia_runs/fixpilot
#
# Pass criteria (all four must hold before scaling up):
#   1. verify_run --diagnose shows NO `x` cells (no seed at the 0.50/0.50 coin flip).
#   2. per-combo spread of approval_rate_M_cumulative across the 3 seeds < 0.15
#      (no spread WARNING from --diagnose).
#   3. probe_policies reports NO FLAT policies (every net's Beta mean varies
#      with its inputs; std across the synthetic batch >= 0.01). SAT rows are
#      worth a look but a confident head near +7 can be legitimate.
#   4. lambda MOVES: --diagnose's lambda table should show few MAXPIN/EPSPIN
#      cells. lambda is learned by dual ascent against the fixed Table 1
#      thresholds in loan_simulator/reward.py (CONSTRAINT_TARGETS, anchored
#      to the coin-flip lender) and is reset to its init at deploy start, so
#      a cell pinned at the cap for the whole deploy means the threshold is
#      unreachable for that policy, one pinned at the floor means it is slack.
#
# NOTE: verify_run.py's completeness check expects the full 13-combo grid, so
# its "checkpoints complete" line will FAIL for this 6-combo pilot -- ignore
# that one line; the --diagnose table and probe are what this pilot is for.

executable = $ENV(HOME)/LoanSimulator/cluster/run_job.sh
arguments  = $(AGENT) $(SEED) $(REWARD) $(CONSTRAINT)

output = $ENV(HOME)/eutopia_logs/pilot_fix_$(ClusterId).$(ProcId).out
error  = $ENV(HOME)/eutopia_logs/pilot_fix_$(ClusterId).$(ProcId).err
log    = $ENV(HOME)/eutopia_logs/pilot_fix_$(ClusterId).log

initialdir = $ENV(HOME)/LoanSimulator

request_cpus   = 2
request_memory = 8192
request_disk   = 5242880
request_gpus   = 0

getenv = True
max_retries = 3

queue AGENT,SEED,REWARD,CONSTRAINT from $ENV(HOME)/LoanSimulator/cluster/pilot_fix_combos.txt
